Z||000005||Oreif||09-18-2001||02:23 AM||||Well if you want to waste a weekend,<P>Tora, Tora, Tora. (Pearl Harbor Attack)<BR>Destination Tokyo. (pre Doolittle raid)<BR>30 Seconds over Tokyo (Doolittle Raid)<BR>Midway (Where we won our first major battle)<BR>Sands of Iwo Jima. (JOhn Wayne..Need I say more?)<BR>The Flying Tigers (see above)<BR>Das Boat<BR>U-571<BR>Sink the Bismark<BR>Dirty Dozen<BR>Kelly's Hero's<BR>Battle of Britain<BR>Patton<BR>Guns of Navarone<BR>Stalag 17<BR>12 O'Clock High<P>There was also a movie about a Destroyer and a U-boat where at the end the 2 ships collide and the 2 captains meet across the burning ships. I think it was a 60's movie.<BR>The entire movie showed both sides and how they each tried to out-smart the other.<BR>I think Robert Mitchum was the destroyer captain.<P><BR>That should keep ya busy a while.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Found it! 1957 "The Enemy Below"<BR><p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 09-18-2001).]||||reg||1
