Z||000014||Fformula88||09-18-2001||08:34 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by maryjane:<BR><B>Apocalypse now- pretty dark, but makes you wonder.<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Stupid me looking for a distraction this weekend went to the theatre to see Apocalypse Now Redux.  Its a re-released version with 53 minutes of extra footage!  Great movie, but very disheartening and depressing.  The Vietnam War sure sucked, and hopefully our gov't doesn't land us in more the same.<P>I also think Platoon is another great war movie!<P>I saw Saving Private Ryan when it came out, and don't think I could stand watching it again.  Another excellent movie, but for me once is enough.<P><P>------------------<BR>John  <BR>AOLIM: Fformula88<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Fiero2m6siga.JPG">     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/halfpole.gif"> <P>1988 Fiero Formula<BR>1985 Fiero SE 2M6||||reg||1
Z||000015||maryjane||09-18-2001||08:45 PM||||forgot about this one. really great. Zulu!||||reg||1
Z||000016||Wolfhound||09-18-2001||09:09 PM||||Apocalypse Now was some kind of science fiction set in Vietnam. had little or nothing to do with reality.<BR> Platoon was also fiction, not realistic at all. It also did the Vietnam Veteran a real disservice. Oliver Stone was rear echelon with the 2/12th and never saw combat, Yet claimed the movie was his own experience.<BR>It was portrayed as the most realistic Vietnam movie yet. When it was first released I took some friends to see it because I wanted them to see what Vietnam was like around Cu Chi. The 2/12th Like my unit (1/27th Wolfhounds)was also in the 25th Division. If I could have got my hands on him when I left the theater I would have deboned his ass.<BR>The most realistic Vietnam scene was the short segment in Forest Gump where they get hit. ||||reg||1
