Z||000019||maryjane||09-18-2001||11:01 PM||||You are right about that, Wolfhound, I always tell people, if they want a small inkling of what a firefight is really like, watch that movie. Everything is there but the smells and the loss of time. Always seem to happen so fast, but sometimes you lose track of time and it's really an hour or longer. They did a good job tho.<BR> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Wolfhound:<BR><B>Apocalypse Now was some kind of science fiction set in Vietnam. had little or nothing to do with reality.<BR> Platoon was also fiction, not realistic at all. It also did the Vietnam Veteran a real disservice. Oliver Stone was rear echelon with the 2/12th and never saw combat, Yet claimed the movie was his own experience.<BR>It was portrayed as the most realistic Vietnam movie yet. When it was first released I took some friends to see it because I wanted them to see what Vietnam was like around Cu Chi. The 2/12th Like my unit (1/27th Wolfhounds)was also in the 25th Division. If I could have got my hands on him when I left the theater I would have deboned his ass.<BR>The most realistic Vietnam scene was the short segment in Forest Gump where they get hit. </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>||||reg||1
