Z||000021||MrPBody||09-19-2001||04:11 PM||||<I>Full Metal Jacket</I> is two movies: one about Boot Camp, and another about Vietnam.  I can't speak for 'Nam reality, because I went to Okinawa instead.  (And I didn't complain about that!)  However, the first section portrays Boot Camp better than any other movie I've seen, although truth is grubbier than the movie.<P>Other good ones, if my failing memory serves:<P>&gt; <I>Saving Private Ryan</I><BR>&gt; <I>Last of the Mohicans</I>  Not modern war, but still war<BR>&gt; <I>Memphis Belle</I><BR>&gt; <I>Das Boot</I><BR>&gt; <I>M*A*S*H</I>  War can be funny<BR>&gt; <I>Kelly's Heros</I>  -- ditto --<BR>&gt; <I>Mister Roberts</I>  -- ditto --<BR>&gt; <I>The Dam Busters</I>  At the time, I thought is was good; now I might think it's hokey<BR>&gt; <I>Schindler's List</I><BR>||||reg||1
